tric reference epoch of that survey, not the universal date of all measurements. Multi-epoch sky positions are conventional catalogue centres.","Error arrays give [lower, upper] absolute one-sigma-equivalent published uncertainty magnitudes. Scalar Error fields take the larger side for asymmetric estimates. Explicit separate random and systematic errors are combined in quadrature when available. Different publications use different error conventions. No homogeneous covariance matrix is assumed.","An extrapolated straight segment is the short-time constant-velocity approximation about the present, as seen from an inertial observer instantaneously co-moving with the Sun. It is not a gravitational orbit or a collision prediction. Uncertainties can make individual transverse components consistent with zero.","Coverage is the 24 external galaxies selectable in this atlas. M32 and M110 have radial-only measurements in the chosen data. The Galactic centre is the origin of the separate Galactocentric solar model."]}
